# Who GitHub asks to review what. GOVERNANCE.md is the rule; this file is how GitHub is told about it.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING IT. `main` has no branch protection — checked against the API on
# 20 September 2026: no required reviews, no required checks, no push restriction. Without a protected
# branch a CODEOWNERS file REQUESTS a reviewer and enforces nothing; a merge with no review is still a
# merge. docs/decisions/2026-09-20-governance.md lists the settings that would make these lines real.
#
# The paths below are GOVERNANCE.md's "two maintainers" row, and they share one reason: a household
# updates by running `planetai update` and cannot review what arrives. init.sql runs against a database
# holding a year of somebody's readings; `install` and `update.sh` are executed by a stranger straight
# off a URL; bin/planetai is what a keeper types when something is already wrong.
#
# Two reviews is the intent and ONE OWNER IS LISTED, because a rule needs somebody who has agreed to
# it. @lucfabcity already holds admin here and is `proposed` in MAINTAINERS.md; uncommenting his name
# on these lines is the one edit that makes the rule two-of-two, and it is his to agree to first.

# Everything, until the list below narrows it.
*                       @tomasdiez

# The schema a node applies to its own database on every update.
/init.sql               @tomasdiez
# /init.sql             @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed — see MAINTAINERS.md

# The contracts §1 names, which node #7 has to share with node #1.
/SPEC.md                @tomasdiez
# /SPEC.md              @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed

# The wire formats' top-level shape. tools/check_wire.py fails when these and the code disagree; that
# gate is what makes a change deliberate, and this is what makes it reviewed. The directory arrives
# with PR #95; a CODEOWNERS path that does not exist yet is harmless and matches nothing until it does.
/tests/data/wire/       @tomasdiez
# /tests/data/wire/     @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed

# What a stranger pipes into bash, and what every node runs to update itself.
/install                @tomasdiez
/install.sh             @tomasdiez
/update.sh              @tomasdiez
# /install              @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed — the installer is his scope
# /install.sh           @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed
# /update.sh            @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed

# The command a keeper types when something is already wrong.
/bin/planetai           @tomasdiez
# /bin/planetai         @tomasdiez @lucfabcity      # proposed

# Governance itself, so a change to who decides is not a one-line PR nobody looked at.
/GOVERNANCE.md          @tomasdiez
